      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm studying for my con law exam and im a bit stuck on judicial philosophy. can u explain what the main arguments are for originalism in constitutional interpretation? like, what are the actual legal justifications for it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Originalism argues that the Constitution should be interpreted according to its original public meaning at the time of enactment to maintain democratic legitimacy and ensure stability. Proponents claim this method respects the rule of law by binding current judges to the will of the people who engaged in the rigorous deliberation of the founding era. By limiting judicial discretion, it prevents unelected judges from posing \"legislative policy\" and overstepping their constitutional authority. Ultimately, this approach aims to create a consistent, predictable legal system grounded in the text and understandings the Founding Fathers intended.",
